# Corpus files must check out byte-for-byte identical regardless of a
# cloning user's core.autocrlf setting -- an LF->CRLF rewrite wouldn't
# corrupt the deliberate Unicode content (zero-width/bidi chars aren't
# newlines), but it would silently change the file's bytes/hash across
# clones, defeating "versioned, immutable" corpus files. Same lesson as
# prompt-firewall's own en_core_web_md CRLF fix (2026-09-08).
corpus/*.jsonl -text

# Test fixtures (e.g. the recorded v1 per-case results Test 23 scores) are
# frozen inputs too.
tests/fixtures/**/*.jsonl -text
